\newlabel{fig:matrix-phases}{{2}{13}{Two-Dimensional problems with the same listed summaries but different curvature/noise pairings, using the discrete sampling law. Left: all four zero-start final-window error displays, with approximate simultaneous 95\% error bars for the 432 primary quantities (often smaller than the symbols). Lines connect observed means; no exponent is fitted. Right: every terminal state at the finest step, retaining all 256 zero-start replicas for each method/pairing. The inset shows the clouds near the minimum. These plots do not prove switching between states or convergence to stationarity. The error separation for smooth sampling distributions is proved separately. Plotting code was developed with OpenAI Codex; displayed quantities are derived from recorded numerical outputs}{figure.2}{}}
